## LLM Prompt Series for Code Generation

Each prompt builds on the previous step, ensures context continuity, and ends by wiring generated code into the existing project. Follow iterative prompt-engineering best practices (provide context, expect small increments, refine prompts ([towardsai.net](mdc:https:/towardsai.net/p/data-science/prompt-engineering-best-practices-iterative-prompt-development?utm_source=chatgpt.com), [arxiv.org](mdc:https:/arxiv.org/abs/2503.11085?utm_source=chatgpt.com))).

### Prompt 1: Scaffold Storybook in Angular

```text
You are an expert Angular developer integrating Storybook. The project uses Angular CLI v14,
TypeScript, and default folder structure. Please:
1. Verify Node.js (>=14) and npm (>=6) versions.
2. Install @storybook/angular, @storybook/cli, @storybook/addon-essentials as devDependencies.
3. Add npm scripts “storybook” and “build-storybook” to package.json.
4. Provide the terminal commands and show the updated package.json section.
Respond with code snippets only, no explanations.
```

### Prompt 2: Configure Storybook Main & Preview

```text
Project now has Storybook installed with scripts. Configure Storybook:
1. Create .storybook/main.js with framework '@storybook/angular', stories pointing to src/**/*.stories.ts, and addons essentials, a11y, viewport.
2. Create .storybook/preview.js to import global CSS and wrap all stories with the AppThemeProvider.
Return the two JS files content.
```

### Prompt 3: Create CSF Stories for Atomic Components

```text
Storybook is configured. Author CSF v3 stories for ButtonComponent:
- Title: 'Atoms/Button'
- Display props: label (string) and disabled (boolean)
- Log click events
Generate src/app/button/button.stories.ts with imports, Meta, Story, and Primary, Disabled examples wired into existing ButtonComponent.
```

### Prompt 4: Add MDX Docs for Card Component

```text
Add documentation for CardComponent:
1. Create src/app/card/card.stories.mdx
2. Include Meta title 'Molecules/Card', import <Props>.
3. Write a markdown overview of Card usage, embed <Props> table, and a default <Story> showing card with title and description.
Provide the MDX content.
```

### Prompt 5: Integrate Accessibility & Viewport Addons

```text
Set up a11y and viewport tests:
1. In .storybook/main.js, ensure '@storybook/addon-a11y' and '@storybook/addon-viewport' are in addons.
2. Create a story for InputComponent error state demonstrating keyboard navigation and ARIA labels.
Return updated main.js and src/app/input/input.stories.ts snippet.
```

### Prompt 6: Setup Chromatic CI for Visual Regression

```text
Integrate Chromatic:
1. Add Chromatic GitHub Action in .github/workflows/storybook.yml to run on pull_request and push to main.
2. Use CHROMATIC_PROJECT_TOKEN env var.
3. Show YAML action snippet.
```

### Prompt 7: Deploy to GitHub Pages

```text
Deploy storybook-static to GitHub Pages:
1. Add JamesIves/github-pages-deploy-action to .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
2. Configure action to publish storybook-static from main branch.
3. Provide the YAML configuration.
```

### Prompt 8: Document SemVer & Maintenance Instructions

```text
Finalize README.md:
1. Add section 'Viewing Storybook' with URL to GitHub Pages.
2. Note SemVer tagging process: tag releases with `vX.Y.Z` and update docs accordingly.
3. Add quarterly cleanup checklist.
Return updated README.md content.
```
